Rast wrote:
> The problem with your current system is that there aren't enough interesting
> categories to compete in, and no runners-up or objective trophies.  For
> instance, there is only one slot that rewards fast ascension.  Players who
> can't do it in less than 15k turns have no hope at all, and so should ignore
> the turn counter entirely, because turn count doesn't matter for *anything*
> else.  Similarly, only one slot exists to reward conducts; if you can't do
> at least seven, you are wasting your time trying any.

This is very true. Runners up should be given a percentage of the
points. Second place would get 50%, third place 25%, fourth place 10%.
You could also force it so a player can only place once, to encourage
more people to go for the trophies.

> Virtually all the non-junk awards are for putting together long strings of
> ascensions (I'll ignore the huge cheating possibilities currently present in
> this category because they *could* be fixed).  These require both very high
> ascension rates and plenty of free time.  The vast majority of players --
> even good players -- don't have those, so they might as well stop playing
> after getting their D. Star or Birdie.

Also very true, though I'd prefer to fix the regular trophies (one
winner each) before fixing achievement trophies (anyone can win).

> How I would do it:
> - Give 1 point (as a base) for each and *every* ascension.

Sure.

> - Dump the Dilithium Star.

I disagree. Many people like the achievement trophies as they are
